      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's not advisable to take Sudafed regularly as it may cause serious side effects, including high blood pressure, which can be dangerous given your condition. Continue taking your lisinopril as prescribed by your doctor. For short-term relief, consider taking acetaminophen or ibuprofen (if you're not allergic and your doctor approves) and rest well. Consult your doctor if your symptoms persist or worsen.",
